- How would you test edge cases like conflicting signals in CI/CD?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical routing under legal constraints that change with jurisdiction, not just prompt quality.

## Key Concepts
- Jurisdiction-aware routing
- Guardrail layering across modules
- Conflict resolution and edge-case handling
- Minimal, testable prototype interfaces

## Code Example
```javascript
// simplified prototype in JS
function route(prompt, jurisdiction){
  const intent = /policy|policy\squery/i.test(prompt) ? 'policy_query' : 'content_action';
  const sensitive = /(SSN|PIN|email)/i.test(prompt);
  let guardrail = jurisdiction === 'GDPR' ? 'minimize personal data processing' : null;
  return { module: 'policy_auto', guardrail };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to enforce data policies in prompt processing, not just theory. It probes edge-case handling and testability.

## Key Concepts
- Prompt safety layering
- Data_sensitivity tagging
- Policy-driven guard rails and auditing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal guard example
function guardPrompt(prompt, policy){
  const intent = parseIntent(prompt);
  const data = tagSensitivity(prompt, policy);
  if(!allowed(data, policy)){ throw new Error('Policy violation'); }
  const guarded = applyGuard(prompt, policy);
  const check = `compliant:${Boolean(guarded)}`;
  return {guardedPrompt: guarded, check};
}
```

